; Equality with a null value gives the same answer with the operands
; swapped.  aux_date is null for a posting that has no auxiliary date;
; with the date on the left, == and != used to fail with "Cannot compare
; a date to an uninitialized value".

2024/01/01 Payee
    A    $5.00
    B

test reg A --format '%(aux_date == [2024/01/01])|%([2024/01/01] == aux_date)|%([2024/01/01] != aux_date)\n'
false|false|true
end test
